@timeline
title: Campaign Timeline

= Campaign Timeline

* **4 February 1949:** attempt on the
  {!<span class="term term-royalist">!}Shah{!</span>!}; martial law,
  arrests, press restrictions, and the ban on the
  {!<span class="term term-left">!}Tudeh Party{!</span>!} follow.
* **Spring 1949:** the constituent assembly strengthens royal authority.
* **October–November 1949:** the palace protest brings the opposition
  coalition that becomes the
  {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}National Front{!</span>!}
  together.
* **18 February 1950:** the Sixteenth
  {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!} opens; the First
  {!<span class="term term-senate">!}Senate{!</span>!} also opens that month.
* **25 November 1950:** the Special Oil Commission rejects the supplemental
  agreement.
* **11 January 1951:** the
  {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!} approves the
  rejection.
* **7–20 March 1951:** {!<span class="term term-independent">!}Razmara{!</span>!}
  is assassinated; the Oil Commission, the
  {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!}, and the
  {!<span class="term term-senate">!}Senate{!</span>!} approve the
  nationalization principle.

{!<a href="timeline.html#the-national-front-and-nationalization-19491951">!}Read
the illustrated chronology{!</a>!}.

