@events
title: Historical Notes

= Historical Notes

## 1949

The attempt on the {!<span class="term term-royalist">!}Shah{!</span>!}
became the occasion for martial law, repression, and constitutional revision.
The October palace protest arose from the disputed
Sixteenth-{!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!} election
and brought together the coalition that became the
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}National Front{!</span>!}.

## 1950

The Tehran rerun returned a small
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}National Front{!</span>!} cohort.
Credentials made that cohort usable in stages. The Special Oil Commission
gave its deputies a forum from which the supplemental agreement could be
examined term by term.

## 1951

The {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!} approved the
commission's rejection of the supplemental agreement on 11 January.
{!<span class="term term-independent">!}Razmara{!</span>!} was assassinated
on 7 March. The commission and both chambers then approved the principle of
oil nationalization, with the
{!<span class="term term-senate">!}Senate{!</span>!} acting on 20 March.

{!<a href="timeline.html#the-national-front-and-nationalization-19491951">!}Dates,
notes, and further reading{!</a>!}.

